# Docker applies .dockerignore from the BUILD CONTEXT ROOT.
#
# The rocketmq-server image context was widened from `server/` to the repository
# root so the Dockerfile's `rmqctl-build` stage can `COPY rmqctl/ ...`. That move
# makes `server/.dockerignore` stop applying, so this root-level file carries its
# intent forward and adds the root-scope directories that would otherwise be
# shipped into the build (hundreds of MB of node_modules / logs / broker data).
#
# DO NOT exclude `server/target/` — deploy.sh mode A builds `--target
# runtime-prebuilt`, which runs `COPY server/target/*.jar app.jar`.
# DO NOT exclude `rmqctl/` — the Go stage needs the module sources (only the
# local build output `rmqctl/bin` is dropped below).

# VCS / CI / hooks
.git
.github
.husky

# IDE & OS noise
.idea
.vscode
*.iml
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Dependencies & front-end build output
**/node_modules
web/dist

# Logs & local Maven repository
**/*.log
server/logs
localRepository

# Local RocketMQ broker runtime data used for manual testing.
# Wildcard, not exact names: on a deployment host this directory gets renamed and
# accumulated — /opt/rocketmq-studio/deploy has been observed holding `rocketmq`,
# `rocketmq-551`, `rocketmq.acl-from-backup` and `rocketmq.disabled-<timestamp>`.
# Nothing else under deploy/ starts with "rocketmq", so the glob is safe.
deploy/rocketmq*
deploy/.env

# ── Secrets must never enter the build context ───────────────────────────────
# The context is the repository root, and a deployment checkout (e.g.
# /opt/rocketmq-studio on the test host) keeps a mode-600 `.env` right there
# holding SPRING_APPLICATION_JSON (plaintext instance admin AK/SK),
# MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD, STUDIO_AUTH_ADMIN_PASSWORD, STUDIO_AI_TOKEN_SECRET and
# RMQ_LLM_TOKEN — plus several timestamped `.env.bak-*` copies of the same, and
# `*.bak-*` backups under deploy/. None of them are matched by any COPY, but they
# would still be packed into the context, handed to the Docker daemon and kept in
# the build cache; with a remote builder configured they would leave the host.
.env
.env.*
**/*.bak-*
# The template is not a secret and is deliberately kept in the context.
!deploy/.env.example

# Local build output only — the rmqctl SOURCES stay in the context
rmqctl/bin
docs/generated
